//? Title: Panoptic FPN things,stuff and quality
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A complete scene description must assign material labels to background pixels while separating each countable object. Panoptic FPN shares features between semantic and instance branches. This report checks overlap resolution and panoptic quality,then visibly fits the complete compact tensor model and inspects actual merged held-out maps.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.7_segmentation/panoptic_fpn.cpp`.

> The method

Shared multiscale features train region proposals,aligned box/mask heads and a group-normalized semantic path. Scored instances claim pixels before semantic stuff fills gaps. Strict-IoU panoptic statistics handle void/crowd and aggregate category counts before quality averages.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/panoptic_fpn_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/panoptic_fpn_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/panoptic_fpn_concept.tikz > build/panoptic_fpn_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/panoptic_fpn_concept.svg build/panoptic_fpn_concept.dvi > build/panoptic_fpn_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
