> Resolve thing overlaps before filling stuff

Panoptic output gives every nonvoid pixel exactly one segment ID and a category.
Countable objects are things;materials such as ground are stuff. The instance
branch supplies scored thing masks,and the semantic branch supplies stuff labels.
In descending score order,an instance is rejected if its already-claimed fraction
exceeds.5;otherwise its claimed pixels are trimmed. Score equality.5 is retained,
and overlap equality.5 is accepted. Empty or fully consumed masks create no
segment. Stuff categories then claim remaining pixels when their area is at
least32. Unclaimed pixels remain void0.

The hand-check below uses a3x4 grid and minimum stuff area2. Mask A claims
four pixels;mask B shares two of its four pixels with A and retains its two
unclaimed pixels. A third heavily overlapping mask is rejected. The remaining
four-pixel stuff region survives while the one-pixel stuff region becomes void.
The exact output IDs are printed as a table;catalogue categories remain separate
from these arbitrary segment IDs.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/panoptic_fpn_merge.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  const auto semantic =
      n::from_vector(std::vector<std::int64_t>{1, 1, 1, 2, 1, 0, 0, 2, 1, 0, 2, 2}, {3, 4});
  std::vector<int> supports(48);
  for (const int i : {0, 1, 4, 5})
    supports[i] = 1;
  for (const int i : {1, 2, 5, 6})
    supports[12 + i] = 1;
  for (const int i : {0, 1, 4})
    supports[24 + i] = 1;
  supports[47] = 1;
  m::TensorMaskDetections masks{{n::zeros({4, 4}), n::tensor({.9, .8, .7, .49}),
                                 n::from_vector(std::vector<std::int64_t>{3, 4, 5, 6}),
                                 n::zeros({4}, n::DType::Int64)},
                                n::not_equal(n::from_vector(supports, {4, 3, 4}), 0.)};
  const auto out = m::MergeTensorPanoptic(semantic, masks, {-1, 10, 11}, .5, .5, 2);
  const auto ids = out.ids.to_vector<int>();
  if (ids != std::vector<int>{1, 1, 2, 3, 1, 1, 2, 3, 0, 0, 3, 3})
    return 1;
  auto a = n::plot_tensor_map(n::reverse(semantic.to(n::DType::Float32), {0}), 0, 3),
       b = n::plot_tensor_map(n::reverse(out.ids.to(n::DType::Float32), {0}), 0, 3);
  a.title("Semantic labels before merging");
  b.title("Resolved segment IDs");
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2).add(a).add(b).size(1100, 480).fit_panels().save_svg(
      "build/panoptic_fpn_merge.svg");
  std::print("| row | column0 | column1 | column2 | column3 |\n|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n");
  for (int row = 0; row < 3; ++row)
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", row, ids[row * 4], ids[row * 4 + 1],
               ids[row * 4 + 2], ids[row * 4 + 3]);
  std::print(
      "Segment1:thing category3;segment2:thing category4;segment3:stuff category11. Exact "
      "overlap equality.5 trims and accepts the second mask. No model or fitting.\n");
}
