> Panoptic quality separates recognition from support accuracy

For a category,only same-category segments at strict IoU greater than.5 match.
Ground-truth void pixels inside a prediction are removed from its match union.
Crowd truth never counts as an ordinary match or false negative;an unmatched
prediction mostly inside void or same-category crowd is ignored. These rules
are checked independently in the native fixtures,including exact-IoU.5 rejection.
For one category,

$$PQ=\frac{\sum_{(p,g)\in TP}IoU(p,g)}{|TP|+|FP|/2+|FN|/2},\quad
SQ=\frac{\sum IoU(p,g)}{|TP|},\quad RQ=\frac{|TP|}{|TP|+|FP|/2+|FN|/2}.$$
\alttext(Panoptic quality divides matched IoU by true positives plus half the false positives and false negatives;segmentation quality measures matched IoU and recognition quality measures detection success.)

Sum category counts over images before macro-averaging categories with any
TP/FP/FN. Per-category PQ equals SQ times RQ,but separately macro-averaged
SQ and RQ need not multiply to macro PQ. Here one three-pixel segment matches
perfectly and another three-pixel truth has only one predicted pixel:TP=1,
FP=1,FN=1,matched IoU=1,PQ=.5,SQ=1,RQ=.5. Segment IDs differ between maps;
matching uses category and support,not ID equality.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/panoptic_fpn_quality.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  m::TensorPanopticMap truth{
      n::from_vector(std::vector<std::int64_t>{1, 1, 1, 2, 2, 2}, {1, 6}),
      {{1, {0, true, false}}, {2, {0, true, false}}}},
      predicted{n::from_vector(std::vector<std::int64_t>{3, 3, 3, 4, 0, 0}, {1, 6}),
                {{3, {0, true, false}}, {4, {0, true, false}}}};
  const auto stats = m::PanopticStatistics(truth, predicted, 1);
  const auto q = m::PanopticQuality(stats, n::ones({1}, n::DType::Bool));
  if (q.pq.item() != .5 || q.sq.item() != 1 || q.rq.item() != .5)
    return 1;
  auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.bars({1, 2, 3}, {q.pq.item(), q.sq.item(), q.rq.item()}, "quality", {37, 99, 235}, .6)
      .title("Known PQ,SQ,RQ")
      .x_label("1:PQ   2:SQ   3:RQ")
      .y_label("category score")
      .y_limits(0, 1.25)
      .size(800, 550);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  p.save_svg("build/panoptic_fpn_quality.svg");
  std::print("Matched IoU1,TP1,FP1,FN1 -> PQ {:.3f},SQ {:.3f},RQ {:.3f}. Strict "
             "IoU>.5;void/crowd/empty-map fixtures pass independently.\n",
             q.pq.item(), q.sq.item(), q.rq.item());
}
```
