> Full shared architecture and initialized gradient census

The source full model shares ResNet50/FPN256 between RPN/aligned box/mask heads
and a GN32 semantic branch of width128. P2/P3/P4/P5 semantic paths use1/1/2/3
3x3/GN/ReLU stages,bilinearly upsample to stride4,and sum before linear scores.
GN has no moving state;ResNet BN does. The complete full256px graph has
46,027,110 learned scalars/all224 gradients. It includes80 foreground instance
classes and54 semantic classes,hidden1024 box head and mask width256.

Compact64px uses ResNet18/divisor8,FPN32,GN8 semantic width16/three classes,
RPN hidden32,box hidden128/11 classes and mask width16/ten foreground classes.
All489,751 learned scalars and125 parameter gradients remain active. The full
initialized execution below checks architecture and differentiation;only the
complete compact model is fitted later.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  n::set_num_threads(2);
  for (bool compact : {false, true}) {
    n::ParameterStore p(17), state(18);
    m::PanopticConfig cfg;
    if (compact) {
      cfg.size = 64;
      cfg.depth = 18;
      cfg.divisor = 8;
      cfg.width = 32;
      cfg.semantic_width = 16;
      cfg.groups = 8;
      cfg.semantic_classes = 3;
      cfg.grayscale = true;
    }
    const int batch = compact ? 2 : 1, channels = compact ? 1 : 3, side = cfg.size;
    const auto image = n::sin(.13 * n::arange(0, batch * side * side * channels))
                           .reshape({batch, side, side, channels});
    const auto features = m::PanopticBackbone(p, state, image, cfg, true);
    const auto rpn = m::BuildPanopticRpn(p, features, compact ? 32 : 256);
    const double s = compact ? 1. : 4.;
    const auto boxes = n::tensor({0., 0., 8. * s, 8. * s, 0., 0., 16. * s, 16. * s, 0., 0.,
                                  32. * s, 32. * s, 0., 0., 64. * s, 64. * s},
                                 {4, 4});
    const auto indices = n::from_vector(compact ? std::vector<std::int64_t>{0, 0, 1, 1}
                                                : std::vector<std::int64_t>{0, 0, 0, 0});
    const auto head = m::PooledDetectionRoiHead(
        p, m::PanopticRoiAlign(features.pyramid, boxes, indices, side, 7, compact ? 32 : 224),
        compact ? 11 : 81, compact ? 128 : 1024);
    const auto masks = m::MaskRcnnHead(
        p, m::PanopticRoiAlign(features.pyramid, boxes, indices, side, 14, compact ? 32 : 224),
        compact ? 16 : 256, compact ? 10 : 80);
    auto loss = n::zeros({});
    for (const auto &value : {features.semantic, rpn.objectness, rpn.deltas,
                              head.probabilities, head.deltas, masks})
      loss = loss + n::mean(n::square(value));
    const auto gradient = n::grad(loss, p.parameters());
    for (const auto &g : gradient)
      if (!g.defined() || !std::isfinite(n::sum(n::square(g.to(n::DType::Float64))).item()) ||
          (compact && n::sum(n::square(g)).item() <= 0))
        return 1;
    if (p.count() != (compact ? 489751 : 46027110) ||
        gradient.size() != std::size_t(compact ? 125 : 224))
      return 1;
    std::print("{} complete Panoptic FPN:{} learned/{} BN state scalars,all{} gradients "
               "at{}px. GN semantic state is learned affine only,no moving moments.\n",
               compact ? "Compact" : "Full", p.count(), state.count(), gradient.size(), side);
  }
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
Full complete Panoptic FPN:46027110 learned/53120 BN state scalars,all224 gradients at256px. GN semantic state is learned affine only,no moving moments.
Compact complete Panoptic FPN:489751 learned/1200 BN state scalars,all125 gradients at64px. GN semantic state is learned affine only,no moving moments.
// result_end

> Actual objects over textured materials

First2048 training-source MNIST digits generate64 fitting/16 validation scenes,
seed11. First512 test-source digits generate eight test scenes,seed22. Digits
retain individual resampled-byte>32 supports,boxes,classes and intensities.
Only nonsupport pixels receive two textured materials,with byte bases40/100
and deterministic0..10 variation. A near-midpoint material split varies by scene.
Semantic targets are0 all things,1/2 the two materials;panoptic categories are
0..9 digits and10/11 materials. Native all-pixel checks ensure supports and
intensities survive synthesis and the stuff target matches its photometry.
This deliberately easy material cue is a teaching task,not a realistic scene
or a benchmark segmentation dataset.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/panoptic_fpn_data.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;

  std::filesystem::path cache;
  if (const auto *p = std::getenv("DATAMUNGE_DATA_DIR"))
    cache = p;
  else if (const auto *p = std::getenv("XDG_CACHE_HOME"))
    cache = std::filesystem::path(p) / "datamunge/datasets";
  else
    cache = std::filesystem::path(std::getenv("HOME")) / ".cache/datamunge/datasets";
  dm::datasets::fetch("mnist", (cache / "mnist").string());

  const auto digits = n::load_mnist((cache / "mnist").string(), "train");
  const auto data =
      m::MakeTensorPanopticScenes(n::slice_axis(digits.images, 0, 0, 2048),
                                  n::slice_axis(digits.labels, 0, 0, 2048), 80, 11);
  std::vector<n::Tensor> sheet;
  for (int row = 0; row < 4; ++row) {
    const auto input =
        n::slice_axis(data.instances.images, 0, row, row + 1) * n::ones({1, 1, 1, 3});
    const auto target = n::slice_axis(data.semantic, 0, row, row + 1);
    const auto categories = n::where(n::equal(target, 0.), n::full({}, -1., n::DType::Int64),
                                     target + n::full({}, 9., n::DType::Int64));
    sheet.push_back(
        n::concat({input, m::ColorPanopticCategories(categories),
                   m::ColorPanopticMap(data.panoptic[row]).reshape({1, 64, 64, 3})},
                  2));
  }
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  n::save_image_grid(n::concat(sheet, 0), "build/panoptic_fpn_data.png", 1, 0, 1, 4, 1., 3);
  std::print("80 actual textured64px scenes:64 fit/16 validation. Each row is input,semantic "
             "target,panoptic truth. Semantic0 all things is black;stuff10 blue-grey/stuff11 "
             "tan,digits retain their ten-class palette. Texture never redefines the original "
             "object supports.\n");
}
```
