\caption(Four unregularized task components and validation box AP50 selection. The code visibly optimizes the entire compact model and restores learned/BN stores together before semantic,instance and merged-map evaluation.)
\alttext(Four unregularized task components and validation box AP50 selection. The code visibly optimizes the entire compact model and restores learned/BN stores together before semantic,instance and merged-map evaluation.)

The selected epoch32 has validation box AP50.063308. Held-out semantic
mean IoU.735548 and stuff PQ.910225 reflect the easy material cues,but thing
PQ and integral mask AP50 are both zero. Test box AP50 is.113274. Overall
category-macro PQ.165495 averages active stuff and missed thing categories;
it does not establish successful instance segmentation. The actual merged
maps below retain the missed objects and void regions.

\image(figures/panoptic_fpn_predictions.png)
\caption(First four actual held-out input/predicted-semantic/true-panoptic/predicted-panoptic quadruples. Semantic things/void are black;two stuff categories use blue-grey/tan and digit categories retain their palette. Colours identify category,while separate segment IDs retain individual objects. Missed,extra and wrong-class masks remain visible.)
\alttext(Four real held-out textured digit scenes with semantic predictions and true versus merged predicted panoptic category maps.)

> Conclusion

Exact overlap,PQ and routed-gradient checks precede complete full-model differentiation and compact fitting. Visible four-task Adam,paired BN restoration,independent held-out masks and merged maps expose recognition and support errors separately. The material cues are deliberately simple teaching data;no pretrained panoptic benchmark result is claimed.

> References

- [Kirillov,Girshick,He and Dollár(2019),Panoptic Feature Pyramid Networks](https://arxiv.org/abs/1901.02446).
- [Kirillov et al.(2019),Panoptic Segmentation](https://arxiv.org/abs/1801.00868).
- [Official panoptic evaluator](https://github.com/cocodataset/panopticapi/blob/master/panopticapi/evaluation.py).
